concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-22-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "22(7) Meetings of the Board"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-22-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) At a meeting of the Board: (a) a quorum is constituted by: (i) if there are not more than 6 non-executive Directors holding office under section 12—4 Directors; or (ii) if there are more than 6 non-executive Directors holding office under that section—5 Directors; (b) all questions shall be decided by a majority of the votes of the Directors present; and (c) the Director presiding has a deliberative vote and, in the event of an equality of votes, also has a casting vote." ;
    skos:definition "(7) At a meeting of the Board: (a) a quorum is constituted by: (i) if there are not more than 6 non-executive Directors holding office under section 12—4 Directors; or (ii) if there are more than 6 non-executive Directors holding office under that section—5 Directors; (b) all questions shall be decided by a majority of the votes of the Directors present; and (c) the Director presiding has a deliberative vote and, in the event of an equality of votes, also has a casting vote."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "669cb30e50ffd50db25e002c823be736046f667a731057da50de12fc4e0b4749" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-22 ;
