concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24 Delegation by Managing Director"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Managing Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate to an employee of the Corporation all or any of his or her powers under this Act, the regulations or the rules, other than this power of delegation. (2) A power delegated under this section, when exercised by the delegate, shall, for the purposes of this Act, the regulations or the rules, be deemed to have been exercised by the Managing Director.   The Board of Directors and the Managing Director  Part III  Section 24 Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 Compilation date: 18/02/2022 Registered: 23/02/2022 (3) A delegation under this section does not prevent the exercise of a power by the Managing Director." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Managing Director may, either generally or as otherwise provided by the instrument of delegation, by writing signed by him or her, delegate to an employee of the Corporation all or any of his or her powers under this Act, the regulations or the rules, other than this power of delegation. (2) A power delegated under this section, when exercised by the delegate, shall, for the purposes of this Act, the regulations or the rules, be deemed to have been exercised by the Managing Director.   The Board of Directors and the Managing Director  Part III  Section 24 Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 Compilation date: 18/02/2022 Registered: 23/02/2022 (3) A delegation under this section does not prevent the exercise of a power by the Managing Director."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6b49244e3042bcf8c788bf24cd0ebe16e826d59533669f209915d72fdb6ff8c2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
