concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24F Appointment of members"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24f ;
    values:originalText "(1) A member of the Nomination Panel is to be appointed by the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department by written instrument. Note: A member of the Nomination Panel may be reappointed: see the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (2) A member holds office on a part-time basis. (3) A member holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years. (4) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department must give notice on the Prime Minister’s Department’s website of each person appointed to the Nomination Panel." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A member of the Nomination Panel is to be appointed by the Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department by written instrument. Note: A member of the Nomination Panel may be reappointed: see the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (2) A member holds office on a part-time basis. (3) A member holds office for the period specified in the instrument of appointment. The period must not exceed 3 years. (4) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department must give notice on the Prime Minister’s Department’s website of each person appointed to the Nomination Panel."@en ;
