concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24N Termination of appointment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24n ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate the appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel for misbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity. (2) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate the appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel if:   Merit-based appointment of non-executive Directors  Part IIIA Constitution and membership of Nomination Panel  Division 2 Section 24P Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 Compilation date: 18/02/2022 Registered: 23/02/2022 (a) the member: (i) becomes bankrupt; or (ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors; or (iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or (iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her creditors; or (b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3 consecutive meetings of the Nomination Panel; or (c) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 24K or 24L (disclosure of interests)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate the appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel for misbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity. (2) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate the appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel if:   Merit-based appointment of non-executive Directors  Part IIIA Constitution and membership of Nomination Panel  Division 2 Section 24P Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 Compilation date: 18/02/2022 Registered: 23/02/2022 (a) the member: (i) becomes bankrupt; or (ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors; or (iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or (iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her creditors; or (b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3 consecutive meetings of the Nomination Panel; or (c) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 24K or 24L (disclosure of interests)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "60b1db8c7ada5530df7a5863304b9bd2ab86f27d7338cd473c865e3004fa7d2f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24n-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24n-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.38" .
doc:sec-24n a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "24N Termination of appointment" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate the appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel for misbehaviour or physical or mental incapacity. (2) The Secretary of the Prime Minister’s Department may terminate the appointment of a member of the Nomination Panel if:   Merit-based appointment of non-executive Directors  Part IIIA Constitution and membership of Nomination Panel  Division 2 Section 24P Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 Compilation date: 18/02/2022 Registered: 23/02/2022 (a) the member: (i) becomes bankrupt; or (ii) applies to take the benefit of any law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors; or (iii) compounds with his or her creditors; or (iv) makes an assignment of his or her remuneration for the benefit of his or her creditors; or (b) the member is absent, except on leave of absence, from 3 consecutive meetings of the Nomination Panel; or (c) the member fails, without reasonable excuse, to comply with section 24K or 24L (disclosure of interests)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer .

