concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-24t a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24T Voting at meetings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-24t ;
    values:originalText "(1) At a meeting of the Nomination Panel, a question is decided by a majority of the votes of members present and voting. (2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, in the event of an equality of votes, also has a casting vote." ;
    skos:definition "(1) At a meeting of the Nomination Panel, a question is decided by a majority of the votes of members present and voting. (2) The person presiding at a meeting has a deliberative vote and, in the event of an equality of votes, also has a casting vote."@en ;
