concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31 Advertisements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31 ;
    values:originalText "Broadcasting services (1) The Corporation shall not broadcast advertisements on any of the Corporation’s broadcasting services. (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the Corporation, if the Board thinks fit, from broadcasting: (a) any announcement relating to any activity or proposed activity of the Corporation; (b) a program supplied by any organization or person engaged in artistic, literary, musical or theatrical production or in educational pursuits; or (c) a program supplied by any organization or person other than a program that is, in the opinion of the Corporation, being used as an advertisement; or from broadcasting any matter the broadcasting of which is directed by the Minister pursuant to subsection 78(1). (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to: (a) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s international television service and its associated audio channels outside Australia; or (b) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s international television service and its associated audio channels inside Australia that is merely incidental to the broadcasting of the matter outside Australia." ;
    skos:definition "Broadcasting services (1) The Corporation shall not broadcast advertisements on any of the Corporation’s broadcasting services. (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the Corporation, if the Board thinks fit, from broadcasting: (a) any announcement relating to any activity or proposed activity of the Corporation; (b) a program supplied by any organization or person engaged in artistic, literary, musical or theatrical production or in educational pursuits; or (c) a program supplied by any organization or person other than a program that is, in the opinion of the Corporation, being used as an advertisement; or from broadcasting any matter the broadcasting of which is directed by the Minister pursuant to subsection 78(1). (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to: (a) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s international television service and its associated audio channels outside Australia; or (b) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s international television service and its associated audio channels inside Australia that is merely incidental to the broadcasting of the matter outside Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4dfe3e7f5b50ffa144d045a9be98acf6acb7ccaf8cfa3007a820f2f7905431d4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "51"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983.pdf, p.51" .
doc:sec-31 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "31 Advertisements" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Broadcasting services (1) The Corporation shall not broadcast advertisements on any of the Corporation’s broadcasting services. (2) Subsection (1) does not prevent the Corporation, if the Board thinks fit, from broadcasting: (a) any announcement relating to any activity or proposed activity of the Corporation; (b) a program supplied by any organization or person engaged in artistic, literary, musical or theatrical production or in educational pursuits; or (c) a program supplied by any organization or person other than a program that is, in the opinion of the Corporation, being used as an advertisement; or from broadcasting any matter the broadcasting of which is directed by the Minister pursuant to subsection 78(1). (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to: (a) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s international television service and its associated audio channels outside Australia; or (b) the broadcasting of any matter by the Corporation’s international television service and its associated audio channels inside Australia that is merely incidental to the broadcasting of the matter outside Australia." ;
    cof:pageNumber "51"^^xsd:integer .

