    cof:title "31B(4) Matters to be included in corporate plans" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of the application of section 35 of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013 in relation to the Corporation, subsidiary is taken to have the meaning given by subsection (3) of this section, despite the definition of subsidiary in section 8 of that Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-31c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31C Corporate plans to be given to Minister"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31c ;
    values:originalText "As soon as practicable after the Board revises a corporate plan, it must give a copy of the plan to the Minister.   Corporate plans  Part IVA  Section 31C Australian Broadcasting Corporation Act 1983 Compilation date: 18/02/2022 Registered: 23/02/2022 Note: A corporate plan must be given to the responsible Minister and the Finance Minister under subsection 35(1) of the Public Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013." ;
