concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-67 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "67 Moneys of the Corporation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-67 ;
    values:originalText "(1) There are payable to the Corporation such moneys as are appropriated by the Parliament for the purposes of the Corporation. (2) The Finance Minister may give directions as to the amounts in which, and the times at which, moneys referred to in subsection (1) are to be paid to the Corporation." ;
    skos:definition "(1) There are payable to the Corporation such moneys as are appropriated by the Parliament for the purposes of the Corporation. (2) The Finance Minister may give directions as to the amounts in which, and the times at which, moneys referred to in subsection (1) are to be paid to the Corporation."@en ;
