concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78-ss-3a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "78(3A) Power of Minister to give directions to Corporation in the"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-78-ss-3a ;
    values:originalText "(3A) If the Minister is of the opinion that the provision of particular content by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the Minister may direct the Corporation to provide that content on all of its digital media services or on such of them as are specified in the direction. If such a direction is given, the Corporation must provide that content, free of charge, in accordance with the direction." ;
    skos:definition "(3A) If the Minister is of the opinion that the provision of particular content by the Corporation would be in the national interest, the Minister may direct the Corporation to provide that content on all of its digital media services or on such of them as are specified in the direction. If such a direction is given, the Corporation must provide that content, free of charge, in accordance with the direction."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "56615f7565b9610e1a6edadb923d1284a4f93d32ccd4afd0eebb81c49edadc0e" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-broadcasting-corporation-act-1983-sec-78 ;
